<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Klima (Milos)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Klima is a fishing village on the island of Milos (Melos) in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyclades">Cyclades</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, on the north side of the island's large natural harbour. Above it lie the remains of the ancient city of Melos, with its walls, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> and early Christian catacombs, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venus-de-milo">Venus de Milo</a> was found nearby in 1820.</p></div>
